KEY: HELP
SUMMARY: List commands, or HELP TOPIC for one card
BODY:
HELP              LIST EVERY CONSOLE COMMAND
HELP TOPIC        SHOW ONE COMMAND, DIRECTIVE, OR
                  OPCODE CARD BY NAME

INSIDE THE EDITOR, PRESS F1 INSTEAD FOR A LIVE
SEARCH OVER EVERYTHING (OPCODES, DIRECTIVES,
COMMANDS, SHORTCUTS, AND THE PROSE GUIDES).
---
KEY: CLS
ALIASES: CLEAR
SUMMARY: Clear the terminal screen
BODY:
CLS
CLEAR             BOTH CLEAR THE TERMINAL AND
                  RETURN THE CURSOR HOME. NEITHER
                  TAKES ARGUMENTS.
---
KEY: MODE
SUMMARY: Print the active application mode
BODY:
MODE              PRINTS EDITOR OR GAME, WHICHEVER
                  IS CURRENTLY ACTIVE.
---
KEY: EDITOR
SUMMARY: Switch to native Editor mode
BODY:
EDITOR            SWITCH TO EDITOR MODE. SAME
                  EFFECT AS PRESSING F1 AT THE
                  CONSOLE PROMPT.
---
KEY: GAME
SUMMARY: Switch to Game mode
BODY:
GAME              SWITCH TO GAME MODE. SAME EFFECT
                  AS PRESSING F2 AT THE CONSOLE
                  PROMPT.
---
KEY: EXIT
ALIASES: QUIT
SUMMARY: Shut down the whole virtual console
BODY:
EXIT
QUIT              BOTH CLOSE THE FANTICON WINDOW AND
                  END THE PROCESS, THE SAME AS
                  CLOSING THE WINDOW DIRECTLY. ANY
                  DIRTY BATTERY-BACKED SAVE RAM IS
                  FLUSHED FIRST.

THIS IS DIFFERENT FROM THE EDITOR'S FILE > EXIT,
WHICH ONLY LEAVES THE EDITOR FOR THE CONSOLE PROMPT.
---
KEY: ECHO
SUMMARY: Print text
BODY:
ECHO text         PRINTS text FOLLOWED BY A NEWLINE.
---
KEY: VERSION
SUMMARY: Print the Fanticon host version
BODY:
VERSION           PRINTS "FANTICON" FOLLOWED BY THE
                  HOST'S CARGO PACKAGE VERSION.
---
KEY: EXPORT
SUMMARY: Export the current project without toolchains
BODY:
EXPORT WEB       BUILD AND EXPORT AN HTML/WASM PLAYER.
EXPORT WIN64     EXPORT WINDOWS X86_64.
EXPORT WINARM    EXPORT WINDOWS ARM64.
EXPORT LINUX64   EXPORT LINUX X86_64.
EXPORT LINUXARM  EXPORT LINUX ARM64.
EXPORT MACOS     EXPORT A UNIVERSAL MACOS PLAYER.

AN OPTIONAL SECOND ARGUMENT SELECTS THE 8.3 OUTPUT
NAME. OFFICIAL INSTALLS INCLUDE EVERY RUNTIME; RUST,
WASM TOOLS, SDKS, AND THE TARGET OS ARE NOT NEEDED.
---
KEY: COLOR
SUMMARY: Show or set the console BG/FG palette pair
BODY:
COLOR             SHOW THE CURRENT BACKGROUND AND
                  FOREGROUND PALETTE INDEXES.
COLOR BG FG       SET BOTH. INDEXES ARE 0-255 AND
                  ACCEPT DECIMAL, $HEX, OR 0xHEX.
                  APPLIES TO BOTH THE CONSOLE AND
                  THE TEXT EDITOR IMMEDIATELY.

EXAMPLE: COLOR 0 255   (DEFAULT: BLACK ON WHITE-ish
                        FOREGROUND, INDEX 255)
---
KEY: EDIT
SUMMARY: Open the text editor, optionally with a file
BODY:
EDIT              OPEN THE TEXT EDITOR ON A NEW,
                  UNTITLED DOCUMENT.
EDIT FILE.TXT     OPEN THE TEXT EDITOR AND LOAD
                  FILE.TXT FROM THE CURRENT
                  DIRECTORY.

OPENING OR SAVING A .ASM OR .INC FILE TURNS ON
6502 ASSEMBLY MODE (SYNTAX COLOR, FOUR-COLUMN
FORMATTING, F1 CONTEXT HELP).
---
KEY: NEW
SUMMARY: Create a cartridge project directory
BODY:
NEW NAME          CREATES A PROJECT DIRECTORY NAMED
                  NAME CONTAINING A FANTICON.CFG
                  MANIFEST AND A STARTER MAIN.ASM,
                  THEN ENTERS THAT DIRECTORY.

NAME MUST BE A SINGLE 8.3-SAFE WORD WITH NO
SPACES. SEE THE CARTRIDGE PROJECTS GUIDE FOR THE
MANIFEST FORMAT.
---
KEY: ASM
SUMMARY: Assemble one source file to a raw .BIN
BODY:
ASM SOURCE           ASSEMBLE SOURCE, WRITING
                     SOURCE WITH ITS EXTENSION
                     REPLACED BY .BIN.
ASM SOURCE OUTPUT    ASSEMBLE SOURCE, WRITING TO
                     OUTPUT INSTEAD.

ALWAYS PRODUCES A RAW BINARY, EVEN INSIDE A
PROJECT DIRECTORY. USE BUILD WITH NO ARGUMENTS TO
PACKAGE A FULL FANTICON.CFG PROJECT.
---
KEY: BUILD
SUMMARY: Package the project, or ASM one source file
BODY:
BUILD                PACKAGES THE CURRENT DIRECTORY'S
                     FANTICON.CFG PROJECT INTO A
                     VALIDATED .FCN CARTRIDGE.
BUILD SOURCE [OUT]   SAME AS ASM: ASSEMBLES ONE RAW
                     SOURCE FILE INSTEAD.

RUN BUILDS AND LAUNCHES IN ONE STEP.
---
KEY: RUN
SUMMARY: Build and launch, or run an existing cartridge
BODY:
RUN                  BUILDS THE CURRENT FANTICON.CFG
                     PROJECT AND LAUNCHES IT.
RUN CARTRIDGE.FCN    VALIDATES AND LAUNCHES AN
                     EXISTING CARTRIDGE IMAGE.

LAUNCHED FROM THE EDITOR'S BUILD > BUILD & RUN OR
SHIFT+F5, ESCAPE RETURNS TO THE EDITOR AND FLUSHES
BATTERY-BACKED RAM. LAUNCHED DIRECTLY FROM THE
COMMAND LINE, ESCAPE IS IGNORED.
---
KEY: DUMP
SUMMARY: Hex/ASCII dump of a file's bytes
BODY:
DUMP FILE               SHOW THE FIRST 128 BYTES.
DUMP FILE OFFSET         START AT OFFSET.
DUMP FILE OFFSET LEN     SHOW LEN BYTES FROM OFFSET.

OFFSET AND LEN ACCEPT DECIMAL, $HEX, OR 0xHEX.
EIGHT BYTES PER ROW: ADDRESS, HEX BYTES, THEN
PRINTABLE ASCII. ZERO-FILLED BYTES ARE DIMMED.

EXAMPLES:
  DUMP GAME.BIN
  DUMP GAME.BIN $80
  DUMP GAME.BIN 0x100 64
---
KEY: CD
SUMMARY: Change or print the current directory
BODY:
CD                PRINT THE CURRENT DIRECTORY.
CD PATH           CHANGE TO PATH. ACCEPTS / OR \
                  SEPARATORS; .. CANNOT MOVE ABOVE
                  THE FANTICON ROOT.
---
KEY: MKDIR
SUMMARY: Create one directory
BODY:
MKDIR PATH        CREATE ONE NEW DIRECTORY. THE
                  PARENT MUST ALREADY EXIST.
---
KEY: RMDIR
SUMMARY: Remove an empty directory
BODY:
RMDIR PATH        REMOVE PATH. THE DIRECTORY MUST
                  BE EMPTY.
---
KEY: RM
ALIASES: DEL
SUMMARY: Remove one file
BODY:
RM FILE
DEL FILE          BOTH REMOVE EXACTLY ONE FILE.
                  NEITHER TAKES A DIRECTORY OR A
                  WILDCARD.
---
KEY: DIR
ALIASES: LS
SUMMARY: List a directory
BODY:
DIR [PATH]
LS [PATH]         LIST PATH, OR THE CURRENT
                  DIRECTORY WITH NO ARGUMENT.
                  DIRECTORIES ARE MARKED <DIR>.
---
KEY: PLAYNSF
SUMMARY: Play an NSF music file in the editor radio
BODY:
PLAYNSF FILE.NSF [TRACK]   START PLAYBACK. TRACKS
                           ARE NUMBERED FROM ONE;
                           OMITTING TRACK USES THE
                           FILE'S DECLARED START
                           TRACK.

THE NSF RADIO KEEPS PLAYING WHILE MOVING BETWEEN
THE PROMPT AND THE CODE EDITOR, AND SUSPENDS
AUTOMATICALLY WHILE A GAME RUNS.
---
KEY: NSF2MUS
SUMMARY: Convert an NSF track to a .MUS tracker file
BODY:
NSF2MUS IN.NSF OUT.MUS [TRACK]

CONVERTS ONE TRACK OF AN NSF FILE INTO A .MUS
TRACKER RESOURCE THAT CAN BE OPENED AND EDITED
WITH EDIT OUT.MUS.
---
KEY: NSFPLAY
SUMMARY: Resume/start NSF radio playback
BODY:
NSFPLAY           RESUME OR START PLAYBACK OF THE
                  LOADED NSF FILE. SAME ACTION AS
                  F7 IN THE EDITOR.
---
KEY: NSFPAUSE
SUMMARY: Pause NSF radio playback
BODY:
NSFPAUSE          PAUSE PLAYBACK WITHOUT LOSING
                  POSITION.
---
KEY: NSFSTOP
SUMMARY: Stop NSF radio playback
BODY:
NSFSTOP           STOP PLAYBACK. SAME ACTION AS
                  SHIFT+F7 IN THE EDITOR.
---
KEY: NSFNEXT
SUMMARY: Advance to the next NSF track
BODY:
NSFNEXT           ADVANCE TO THE NEXT TRACK. SAME
                  ACTION AS F8 IN THE EDITOR.
---
KEY: NSFPREV
SUMMARY: Go back to the previous NSF track
BODY:
NSFPREV           GO BACK ONE TRACK. SAME ACTION AS
                  SHIFT+F8 IN THE EDITOR.
---
KEY: NSFLOOP
SUMMARY: Toggle one-pass/two-pass NSF loop playback
BODY:
NSFLOOP           TOGGLE BETWEEN PLAYING A DETECTED
                  LOOP ONCE OR TWICE BEFORE
                  ADVANCING TO THE NEXT TRACK.
---
KEY: NSFINFO
SUMMARY: Print the loaded NSF file's current status
BODY:
NSFINFO           PRINT THE CURRENT TRACK, TOTAL
                  TRACKS, PLAY/PAUSE STATE, AND
                  LOOP MODE.
---
